{"abstract":"Whether DNA methylation changes follow human physical trauma is uncertain. We aimed to investigate if severe trauma was associated with DNA methylation changes. In a prospective, observational, clinical study, we included severely injured adults and adults undergoing elective surgery (controls). Blood was obtained from trauma patients (n = 60) immediately- and 30-45 days post-trauma, and from surgical patients (n = 57) pre-, post-, and 30-45 days post-surgery. Epigenome-wide DNA methylation profiling was performed and analyzed for significant differentially methylated CpGs and -regions (DMRs) within and between groups. Within the trauma group we identified 10,126 significant differentially methylated CpGs and 1169 DMRs. No significant differential methylation was found in the surgical group. In the trauma group, differentially methylated sites were enriched in genes and pathways involved in blood coagulation and inflammatory response. Severe trauma was associated with profound alterations in the DNA methylome of circulating leucocytes, and differential methylation was located in trauma-relevant genes.","author_count":16,"contributors":["Eskesen, Trine O.","Almstrup, Kristian","Elgaard, Laurits","Arleth, Tobias","Lassen, Mathilde L.","Creutzburg, Andreas","Jensen, Alice Herrlin","Breindahl, Niklas","Dinesen, Felicia","Vang, Malene","Sørensen, Erik","Paulsen, Anders Wallin","Nielsen, Tatiana","Rasmussen, Lars S","Sillesen, Martin","Steinmetz, Jacob"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-777094"],"filters":{"added":"2025-01","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-OTH"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-OTH","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"severe traumatic injury is associated with profound changes in dna methylation","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41525-024-00438-4","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-777094","identifier":[{"id":"PMC11530621","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"39487175","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85208574066","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-1b09a088-fe50-4e3a-a1b5-d16bfee9fdec"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-D21CDEA01F6891B65388926C1F51C8C7"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41525-024-00438-4","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/411756107/s41525_024_00438_4.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Cellular and Molecular Medicine, Medical Genetics Program"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"other hospitals","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-OTH","l3nl":"Other Hospitals","l3nn":"Other Hospitals","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Other Hospitals","namevar":["Danish Air Ambulance"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-OTH","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Trine O.","key":"eskesenpau","last":"Eskesen","name":"Eskesen, Trine O.","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Kristian","key":"almstruppau","last":"Almstrup","locid":"6dcb9136-f13d-4486-916a-3e29ffb45147","name":"Almstrup, Kristian","orcid":"0000-0002-1832-0307","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Laurits","key":"elgaardpau","last":"Elgaard","name":"Elgaard, Laurits","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Tobias","key":"arlethpau","last":"Arleth","name":"Arleth, Tobias","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Mathilde L.","key":"lassenpau","last":"Lassen","name":"Lassen, Mathilde L.","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Andreas","key":"creutzburgpau","last":"Creutzburg","name":"Creutzburg, Andreas","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Alice Herrlin","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","name":"Jensen, Alice Herrlin","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Niklas","key":"breindahlpau","last":"Breindahl","name":"Breindahl, Niklas","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Felicia","key":"dinesenpau","last":"Dinesen","name":"Dinesen, Felicia","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Malene","key":"vangpau","last":"Vang","name":"Vang, Malene","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Erik","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","name":"Sørensen, Erik","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Anders Wallin","key":"paulsenpau","last":"Paulsen","name":"Paulsen, Anders Wallin","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Tatiana","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Tatiana","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Lars S.","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"37e36b99-34dd-471f-b09b-d93e72940ec0","name":"Rasmussen, Lars S","name_org":"Rasmussen, Lars S.","rank":14,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Martin","key":"sillesenpau","last":"Sillesen","locid":"896857bd-2dfb-4559-8033-b2f9220ab606","name":"Sillesen, Martin","rank":15,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2 3","first":"Jacob","key":"steinmetzpau","last":"Steinmetz","locid":"5a72d483-a14d-40ba-8294-4fefb8ec7755","name":"Steinmetz, Jacob","rank":16,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["39487175"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1038/s41525-024-00438-4","issn":["20567944"],"journal":"npj Genomic Medicine","paperid":"53","status":"p","title":"npj Genomic Medicine","volume":"9"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85208574066"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Other Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen","danish air ambulance"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-1b09a088-fe50-4e3a-a1b5-d16bfee9fdec"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Severe traumatic injury is associated with profound changes in DNA methylation","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-777094","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Background: To facilitate tracheal intubation, either a neuromuscular blocking agent or a bolus dose of remifentanil can be administered. We hypothesized that rocuronium 0.6 mg·kg−1 provided a larger proportion of excellent intubating conditions compared to remifentanil 2 µg·kg−1 in patients above 80 years. Methods: A total of 78 patients were randomized to either rocuronium 0.6 mg·kg−1 or remifentanil 2 µg·kg−1. General anaesthesia was initiated with fentanyl and propofol. Two minutes after the administration of either rocuronium or remifentanil, tracheal intubating conditions were evaluated using the Fuchs-Buder scale by a blinded investigator, and our primary outcome was the proportion of patients presenting intubating conditions deemed as excellent. Further outcomes included the Intubating Difficulty Scale (IDS), hoarseness or sore throat 24 h postoperatively, and intervention against hypotension. Results: No difference in the occurrence of excellent intubating conditions was found comparing the rocuronium group with the remifentanil group; 10 (28%) versus 15 (39%) (p =.29), respectively, relative risk = 0.72. Interventions against hypotension were used in 24 (67%) versus 28 (74%) (p =.51), respectively. Hoarseness and sore throat 24 h postoperatively were found in 37% versus 35% p =.86, and 14% versus 5% p =.20, respectively. The IDS score was 2 versus 2 p =.48. Conclusion: No difference in intubating conditions was found 2 min after the administration of either rocuronium 0.6 mg·kg−1 or remifentanil 2 µg·kg−1 in patients aged above 80 years. Intubation conditions were less than optimal in a large proportion of this patient population. Clinical trials registration: NCT04287426.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Vested, Matias","Sørensen, Anne Marie","Bjerring, Cecilie","Christensen, Rasmus E.","Dinesen, Felicia","Vang, Malene","Gilvanoff, Alexander","Hansen, Thea Ellehammer","Nielsen, Tatiana","Rasmussen, Lars S"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-530598"],"filters":{"added":"2022-03","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Elderly patients","Neuromuscular blocking agents","Tracheal intubating conditions"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a blinded randomized study comparing intubating conditions after either rocuronium 000000000000 000000000006 mg kg sup 000000000001 sup or remifentanil 000000000002 µg kg sup 000000000001 sup in elderly patients","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-530598","identifier":[{"id":"85114359226","type":"scopus"},{"id":"34310692","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-e5b299c6-3035-43e3-9c05-4b41305bd941"],"keyword":["elderly patients","neuromuscular blocking agents","tracheal intubating conditions"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-B001354B60389308733FA26B5E1B79DB"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Anaesthesiology","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Hea