{"affno":"2","first":"Lotte Riis","key":"andersenlotteriispau","last":"Andersen","name":"Andersen, Lotte Riis","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jørgen","key":"delmanjørgenpau","last":"Delman","locid":"f0fd2027-7333-420e-94be-8e066bd8bb61","name":"Delman, Jørgen","orcid":"0000-0002-8987-2248","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Kjeld Erik","key":"brødsgaardkjelderikpau","last":"Brødsgaard","name":"Brødsgaard, Kjeld Erik","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Andreas Bøje","key":"forsbyandreasbøjepau","last":"Forsby","locid":"bed2c122-a6b5-42bb-8b9c-50d83926b36c","name":"Forsby, Andreas Bøje","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Kristian Søby","key":"kristensenkristiansøbypau","last":"Kristensen","locid":"271c23b9-c5b2-49d9-9b0f-b55a9340e189","name":"Kristensen, Kristian Søby","orcid":"0000-0002-2555-8014","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Bertel","key":"heurlinbertelpau","last":"Heurlin","locid":"b5c6ae89-afac-44e6-8fd1-9c2c1a252a30","name":"Heurlin, Bertel","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Jacobsen","key":"andrékenjacobsenpau","last":"André Ken","name":"André Ken, Jacobsen","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Peter Marcus","key":"kristensenpetermarcuspau","last":"Kristensen","locid":"77541a90-f915-457d-b134-46acbcd60b84","name":"Kristensen, Peter Marcus","orcid":"0000-0002-8357-5293","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Ole","key":"wæverolepau","last":"Wæver","locid":"616ba573-b094-46ed-a29b-56d8f2a5049e","name":"Wæver, Ole","orcid":"0000-0002-9053-5855","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","first":"Mette","key":"thunømettepau","last":"Thunø","name":"Thunø, Mette","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Cecilia Felicia Stokholm","key":"bankececiliafeliciastokholmpau","last":"Banke","name":"Banke, Cecilia Felicia Stokholm","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Nis Høyrup","key":"christensennishøyruppau","last":"Christensen","name":"Christensen, Nis Høyrup","rank":14,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"pages":"4","publisher":"Center for Militære Studier, Institut for Statskundskab, Københavns Universitet","series":"CMS Notat","status":"p"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Governmental Institutions","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-GV-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Governmental Institutions","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-423aeed4-33fa-4d18-a962-e4aca96e3647"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"CMS Notat: \"Forværringen af det kinesisk-amerikanske forhold: en strategisk udfordring for Danmark\"","type":"Working Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-433021","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"The role of host genetic variation in the development of complicated Staphylococcus aureus bacteremia (SAB) is poorly understood. We used whole exome sequencing (WES) to examine the cumulative effect of coding variants in each gene on risk of complicated SAB in a discovery sample of 168 SAB cases (84 complicated and 84 uncomplicated, frequency matched by age, sex, and bacterial clonal complex [CC]), and then evaluated the most significantly associated genes in a replication sample of 240 SAB cases (122 complicated and 118 uncomplicated, frequency matched for age, sex, and CC) using targeted sequence capture. In the discovery sample, gene-based analysis using the SKAT-O program identified 334 genes associated with complicated SAB at p<3.5 x 10 −3. These, along with eight biologically relevant candidate genes were examined in the replication sample. Gene-based analysis of the 342 genes in the replication sample using SKAT-O identified one gene, GLS2, significantly associated with complicated SAB (p = 1.2 x 10 −4) after Bonferroni correction. In Firth-bias corrected logistic regression analysis of individual variants, the strongest association across all 10,931 variants in the replication sample was with rs2657878 in GLS2 (p = 5 x 10 −4). This variant is strongly correlated with a missense variant (rs2657879, p = 4.4 x 10 −3) in which the minor allele (associated here with complicated SAB) has been previously associated with lower plasma concentration of glutamine. In a microarray-based gene-expression analysis, individuals with SAB exhibited significantly lower expression levels of GLS2 than healthy controls. Similarly, Gls2 expression is lower in response to S. aureus exposure in mouse RAW 264.7 macrophage cells. Compared to wild-type cells, RAW 264.7 cells with Gls2 silenced by CRISPR-Cas9 genome editing have decreased IL1-β transcription and increased nitric oxide production after S. aureus exposure. GLS2 is an interesting candidate gene for complicated SAB due to its role in regulating glutamine metabolism, a key factor in leukocyte activation.","author_count":29,"contributors":["Scott, William K","Medie, Felix Mba","Ruffin, Felicia","Sharma-Kuinkel, Batu K","Cyr, Derek D","Guo, Shengru","Dykxhoorn, Derek M","Skov, Robert L","Bruun, Niels Eske","Dahl, Anders","Lerche, Christian J","Petersen, Andreas","Larsen, Anders Rhod","Lauridsen, Trine Kiilerich","Johansen, Helle Krogh","Ullum, Henrik","Sørensen, Erik","Hassager, Christian","Bundgaard, Henning","Schønheyder, Henrik Carl","Torp-Pedersen, Christian","Oestergaard, Louise Bruun","Arpi, Magnus","Rosenvinge, Flemming","Erikstrup, Lise T","Chehri, Mahtab","Søgaard, Peter","Andersen, Paal S","Fowler, Vance G"],"cuid":["S04-096.54-003121"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":4,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"country":["United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Duke Clinical Research Institute","Duke University","Duke University Medical Center","University of Miami"],"keyword":["Adolescent","Adult","Aged","Aged 80 and over","Alleles","Animals","Bacteremia","Female","Gene Frequency genetics","Genetic Variation genetics","Humans","Male","Mice","Middle Aged","RAW 264 7 Cells","Risk Factors","Staphylococcus aureus pathogenicity","Transcriptome genetics","Whole Exome Sequencing methods"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-SSI"],"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-SDR"],"OT":["Dr. John T. Macdonald Foundation Department of Human Genetics, Miller School of Medicine, University of Miami, Miami, FL, United States of America."],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-GV-SSI","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-SDR","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","